ll,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":1779711,"type":"pull_ref","html_url":"https://gitea.com/gitea/tea/issues/1129#issuecomment-1779711","pull_request_url":"","issue_url":"https://gitea.com/gitea/tea/issues/1129","user":{"id":173651,"login":"bircni","type":"User","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"bircni","email":"173651+bircni@noreply.gitea.com","avatar_url":"https://gitea.com/avatars/9b753b6bef510146768e173e70a1a3904a76262c3a0b95e6579d06976650f3d4","html_url":"https://gitea.com/bircni","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2026-01-25T11:14:23Z","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"following_count":2,"starred_repos_count":2,"username":"bircni"},"body":"","created_at":"2026-10-18T18:12:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T18:12:16Z","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":{"id":512822,"url":"https://gitea.com/api/v1/repos/gitea/tea/issues/1147","html_url":"https://gitea.com/gitea/tea/pulls/1147","number":1147,"user":{"id":173651,"login":"bircni","type":"User","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"bircni","email":"173651+bircni@noreply.gitea.com","avatar_url":"https://gitea.com/avatars/9b753b6bef510146768e173e70a1a3904a76262c3a0b95e6579d06976650f3d4","html_url":"https://gitea.com/bircni","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2026-01-25T11:14:23Z","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"following_count":2,"starred_repos_count":2,"username":"bircni"},"original_author":"","original_author_id":0,"title":"feat: finish the tea 1.0 rewrite — gh-style UX, review fixes, release prep","body":"Second half of the tea 1.0 rewrite. #1122–#1126 landed the Cobra command tree, the\nservices layer on `gitea.dev/sdk`, credentials/Git and the terminal package. This PR\npolishes it into the gh-style CLI the reviewers asked for, fixes what a full review of\nthe branch found, and prepares the 1.0.0 release. It supersedes the revert in #1146.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Output and commands (gh-style)**\n- TTY lists with UPPERCASE headers, columns fitted to the terminal, relative times and\n  `✓` confirmations on stderr; piped output is TSV without header or color.\n- Issue/PR/release/milestone/wiki views render Markdown; `--json`, `--jq` and the field\n  list for unknown fields work on every command.\n- gh flag and alias parity: `ls`/`rm`, `-L -s -l -a -A -m -t -b -F -e -w -S`, `pr review\n  --approve/--request-changes/--comment`, `pr merge` with the repository's defaults,\n  `pr ready`, `pr checks` with gh's exit code, `release upload --clobber`,\n  `run watch/download`, `repo rename/unarchive/fork --remote`, `auth login/status/switch`,\n  `doctor`, `tea status` and `tea api --verbose`.\n- Grouped help, help topics (`environment`, `exit-codes`, `formatting`), flag-value\n  completion and \"did you mean\" for unknown flags.\n\n**Review fixes (about 150 items, each with a regression test)**\n- Security: terminal escape sequences from server text (Markdown character references,\n  PR titles in messages, `auth status`, `notification watch`, JSON/jq output) can no\n  longer reach the terminal; `auth logout` only asks Git to forget tea's own credential.\n- Behavior: `team edit --unit` keeps the access of read/write teams and the owner team\n  cannot be renamed; `release edit --draft false` (0.16 syntax) is refused instead of\n  reversing the release; `release upload --clobber` uploads before deleting; re-login keeps\n  SSH settings; `pr merge` no longer deletes a head branch Gitea kept; `pr checkout`,\n  `pr clean` and the no-argument `pr` commands no longer pick an unrelated fork branch;\n  `review_decision` ignores comment-only reviews; `comment list`/`pr review list` page\n  correctly; wiki edits no longer overwrite an existing page.\n- Where gh solves the same problem the fix follows gh (for example `auth status --json`\n  always exits 0, a bare `GITEA_TOKEN` overrides stored accounts, `pr reopen|close|view`\n  find closed and merged PRs by branch, `release create --verify-tag`).\n\n**Folded in from open PRs**\n- #1021 (find the Gitea remote among all remotes), #1144 (load the `pr create`/`issue\n  create` form data concurrently) and #1145 (single-request template lookup), re-implemented\n  on the new architecture.\n- In a fork clone tea now prefers `upstream` over a tracked `origin` (#338).\n\n**Release prep**\n- goldmark and `golang.org/x` updated (the previous goldmark was flagged by govulncheck);\n  stale `retract` removed; snap build handles lightweight tags; version fallback for\n  builds without ldflags; man pages include the help topics; `CHANGELOG.md` has a drafted\n  1.0.0 section; the integration tests match the 1.0 behavior.\n\n## Breaking changes and migration\n\nEverything that differs from tea 0.16 is documented in `docs/migration-1.0.md` (renamed\ncommands, changed short flags such as `pr create -b`, removed flags, config split, Gitea 28\nrequirement). This PR adds the remaining notes found during review.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\n- `flake.lock` still pins an old nixpkgs (needs `nix flake update nixpkgs`).\n- Larger features stay for 1.1: `issue export/import` (#132), project boards (#435), TLS\n  client certificates (#451), custom login headers (#990), package commands (#843).\n- Open design questions: `team edit --permission` on Gitea 28.0.0, atomic topic updates in\n  `repo edit`, `--repo NAME` matching a local directory name.\n\n## Issues\n\nfixes #69\nfixes #141\nfixes #162\nfixes #172\nfixes #197\nfixes #240\nfixes #246\nfixes #323\nfixes #325\nfixes #326\nfixes #328\nfixes #344\nfixes #351\nfixes #373\nfixes #403\nfixes #406\nfixes #417\nfixes #430\nfixes #457\nfixes #480\nfixes #482\nfixes #489\nfixes #490\nfixes #498\nfixes #500\nfixes #504\nfixes #510\nfixes #516\nfixes #523\nfixes #556\nfixes #560\nfixes #569\nfixes #571\nfixes #632\nfixes #633\nfixes #643\nfixes #672\nfixes #677\nfixes #683\nfixes #697\nfixes #726\nfixes #737\nfixes #770\nfixes #779\nfixes #804\nfixes #817\nfixes #831\nfixes #833\nfixes #834\nfixes #908\nfixes #966\nfixes #1032\nfixes #1050\nfixes #1069\nfixes #1091\nfixes #1094\nfixes #1110\nfixes #1115\nfixes #1116\nfixes #1118\nfixes #407\nfixes #774\nfixes #1129\n","ref":"","assets":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"projects":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":null,"state":"closed","is_locked":false,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-18T12:52:03Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T20:56:21Z","closed_at":"2026-10-18T20:56:21Z","due_date":null,"time_estimate":0,"pull_request":{"merged":false,"merged_at":null,"draft":false,"html_url":"https://gitea.com/gitea/tea/pulls/1147"},"repository":{"id":550,"name":"tea","owner":"gitea","full_name":"gitea/tea"},"pin_order":0,"content_version":1},"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"closes","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":null,"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":1805187,"type":"comment","html_url":"https://gitea.com/gitea/tea/issues/1129#issuecomment-1805187","pull_request_url":"","issue_url":"https://gitea.com/gitea/tea/issues/1129","user":{"id":173651,"login":"bircni","type":"User","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"bircni","email":"173651+bircni@noreply.gitea.com","avatar_url":"https://gitea.com/avatars/9b753b6bef510146768e173e70a1a3904a76262c3a0b95e6579d06976650f3d4","html_url":"https://gitea.com/bircni","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2026-01-25T11:14:23Z","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"fo